> Module Pensoes

# Formal Specification (First-Order Logic)
#
# Domain: B — set of beneficiaries
# Variables: age(b) ∈ ℕ, years(b) ∈ ℕ, for b ∈ B
#
# GP(b) ↔ years(b) ≥ 15                         [Art. 19]
# NA(b) ↔ age(b) ≥ 65                            [Art. 20, original 2007]
# E(b)  ↔ GP(b) ∧ NA(b)                          [Art. 10(1), partial]
#
# Expanded:
# E(b) ↔ years(b) ≥ 15 ∧ age(b) ≥ 65
#
# Scope: DL 187/2007, original wording, before 2014 amendments.
# Excludes: anticipation regimes (Art. 20 a-d), Art. 12 density rules.

# Article 19. Guarantee period

The guarantee period for the award of an old-age pension is 15 civil
years, consecutive or interpolated, with a record of remuneration,
under the terms of article 12.

```catala
declaration scope GuaranteePeriod:
  input years_with_remuneration content integer
  output meets_guarantee_period content boolean

scope GuaranteePeriod:
  definition meets_guarantee_period equals
    years_with_remuneration >= 15
```

# Article 20. Normal age of access to old-age pension
# (original wording, DL 187/2007, before 2014 amendments)

The recognition of the right to an old-age pension further depends on
the beneficiary being aged 65 or over, without prejudice to the
following special anticipation regimes and measures.

```catala
declaration scope NormalAgeAccess:
  input age content integer
  output meets_age_condition content boolean

scope NormalAgeAccess:
  definition meets_age_condition equals
    age >= 65
```

# Article 10, paragraph 1. Common conditions for old-age pension
# (partial -- guarantee period and age only)

The recognition of the right to old-age pensions depends on the
fulfilment of the guarantee period and on the submission of a request.

```catala
declaration scope OldAgePensionEligibility:
  input age content integer
  input years_with_remuneration content integer
  guarantee_period scope GuaranteePeriod
  normal_age scope NormalAgeAccess
  output is_eligible content boolean

scope OldAgePensionEligibility:
  definition guarantee_period.years_with_remuneration equals
    years_with_remuneration
  definition normal_age.age equals
    age
  definition is_eligible equals
    guarantee_period.meets_guarantee_period
    and normal_age.meets_age_condition
```

# Tests

```catala
declaration scope TestCase1:
  output result content OldAgePensionEligibility

scope TestCase1:
  definition result equals
    output of OldAgePensionEligibility with {
      -- age: 68
      -- years_with_remuneration: 35
    }
  assertion result.is_eligible

declaration scope TestCase2:
  output result content OldAgePensionEligibility

scope TestCase2:
  definition result equals
    output of OldAgePensionEligibility with {
      -- age: 50
      -- years_with_remuneration: 20
    }
  assertion not result.is_eligible

declaration scope TestCase3:
  output result content OldAgePensionEligibility

scope TestCase3:
  definition result equals
    output of OldAgePensionEligibility with {
      -- age: 65
      -- years_with_remuneration: 15
    }
  assertion result.is_eligible
```

# Boundary cases. These mirror tests/vectors.json and the Lean examples in
# lean/DL187/Eligibility.lean; the three implementations must agree.

```catala
declaration scope TestCase4:
  output result content OldAgePensionEligibility

scope TestCase4:
  definition result equals
    output of OldAgePensionEligibility with {
      -- age: 64
      -- years_with_remuneration: 40
    }
  assertion not result.is_eligible

declaration scope TestCase5:
  output result content OldAgePensionEligibility

scope TestCase5:
  definition result equals
    output of OldAgePensionEligibility with {
      -- age: 70
      -- years_with_remuneration: 14
    }
  assertion not result.is_eligible

declaration scope TestCase6:
  output result content OldAgePensionEligibility

scope TestCase6:
  definition result equals
    output of OldAgePensionEligibility with {
      -- age: 30
      -- years_with_remuneration: 5
    }
  assertion not result.is_eligible
```
